<p>Mark Gurman has last-minute Apple product details <a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/newsletters/2026-10-11/apple-smart-home-launch-oct-13-plans-homeview-has-mid-november-release">in his Sunday newsletter</a>:</p>
<blockquote><p>
  The centerpiece is a new smart home hub called the HomeView. Equipped with a display and an A18 chip, the product essentially serves as the Siri command center for an Apple-powered household…</p>
<p>  The HomeView comes in two versions: a countertop model with a metal speaker base and a wall-mounted version with a flat, square base that sits against the wall beneath the display. The countertop offering will come in four colors: space gray, silver, starlight and pink, while the wall-mounted version will be limited to space gray and silver.
</p></blockquote>
<p>The name dovetails with a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/09/homeview-trademark/">MacRumors report</a> that Apple used a shell company to trademark “HomeView” last year. So much for <a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2026/10/is-apple-coming-home-to-stay/">my prediction</a> of a re-use of the base HomePod name.</p>
<p>Gurman also says the new Apple TV remote will have a speaker, and the new Apple TV itself will have a microphone to enable it to receive Siri requests directly.</p>
